}


3.. Consideration of Business License Tax Study Results and Feedback from Business License Tax Forum (No Immediate Revenue Impact) (Finance Director Bretthauer).
(Estimated Time: 1.5 Hr.)
DISCUSS AND PROVIDE DIRECTION  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Amy Thomas Howorth {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Mayor Lesser stated that City Councilmembers with a business license may participate in General Business Item No. 3.\line\line City Attorney Quinn Barrow responded to City Council questions.\cf1\i0\line\line\cf0\i Finance Director Libby Bretthauer introduced Financial Services Manager Emy-Rose Hanna who provided the PowerPoint presentation on Business License Tax Modernization Plan Update - Phase 2.\line\line HDL Operations Director Eric Meyers continued the PowerPoint presentation on Preliminary Tax Study Results.\line\line HDL Operations Director Meyers and City Manager Talyn Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line HDL Operations Director Meyers continued the PowerPoint presentation on Model 1 - Gross Receipts Cap Removed.\line\line HDL Operations Director Meyers, Financial Services Manager Hanna, and Finance Director Bretthauer responded to City Council questions.\line\line Financial Services Manager Hanna continued with the PowerPoint presentation on the Last Polling Question from Business License Tax Forum.\line\line Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Tim Ryan\line Stefan Kampe\line Michael Zislis\line Kyle Ransford\line Jill Lamkin\line Chandra Shaw\line Diane Forte\line\line\pard Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line Finance Director Bretthauer and HDL Operations Director Meyers responded to City Council questions.\cf2\i0\f1\fs24\par
}


5.. Presentation of the Fiscal Year 2027 Proposed Operating Budget and Consideration of CERT Funding Request (Continued) (Not Budgeted) (Finance Director Bretthauer). 
(Estimated Time: 1 Hr.)
DISCUSS AND PROVIDE DIRECTION {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Finance Director Libby Bretthauer provided background on the item and began the PowerPoint presentation.\line\line The following staff members provided the PowerPoint overview of their departmental budgets:\line\line\ul Management Services:\ulnone\line Assistant City Clerk Patricia Matson presented.\line\line\ul Finance\ulnone\line Finance Director Bretthauer presented.\line\line\ul Human Resources\ulnone\line Human Resources Director Lisa Jenkins presented.\line\line\ul Parks and Recreation\ulnone\line Parks and Recreation Director Mark Leyman presented.\line\line\ul Police\ulnone\line Police Chief Rachel Johnson presented and responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Fire\ulnone\line Fire Chief Jesse Alexander presented.\line\line Fire Chief Alexander and City Manager Talyn Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Community Development\ulnone\line Community Development Director Masa Alkire presented and responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Public Works\ulnone\line Interim Public Works Director Joseph DeFrancesco presented.\line\line\ul Information Technology\ulnone\line Information Technology Director Miguel Guardado presented and responded to City Council questions.\line\line\pard Finance Director Bretthauer continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Next Steps/Recommendation.\cf1\i0\f1\fs24\par
}


1.. Consideration of Second Reading and Adoption of an Ordinance Amending the Manhattan Beach Municipal Code Relating to Bicycles to: (1) Supplement Safety and Operational Requirements for Electric and Motorized Bicycles; and (2) Institute a Juvenile Diversion Program for Juvenile Violators of the Ordinance (No Budget Impact) (Police Chief Johnson).
ADOPT ORDINANCE NO. 26-0007  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Amy Thomas Howorth {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\cf1\ul\b\fs22 ITEMS REMOVED FROM THE CONSENT CALENDAR\ulnone\b0\i\f1\line\line Mayor Pro Tem Franklin stated that he pulled the item to benefit the public, noting that the ordinance includes additional regulations governing the use of bicycles, including e-bikes. He emphasized that this action is an amendment to existing regulations and confirmed this information to ensure the public is aware of the enhanced requirements.\cf0\b\i0\line\line\b0\i Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments.\line\line\pard Seeing no requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\cf1\i0\f0\fs24\par
}


4.. Resumption of the Presentation of the Proposed Five-Year Capital Improvement Program (CIP) for Fiscal Year 2026-2027 through Fiscal Year 2030-2031 (Not Budgeted) (Interim Public Works Director DeFrancesco).
(Estimated Time: 30 Mins.)
